        "original_id": "41ee55b8-cd11-52e1-948a-449c14b9a1d2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jaroslav Kvapil, Antonín Dvořák\n- Places: Chudenice, Prague, Kingdom of Bohemia, Central Europe\n- Works: Rusalka\n- Concepts: Czech poet, playwright, librettist, medieval monarchy, early modern monarchy, predecessor state\n\nFacts:\n- Jaroslav Kvapil was born on 25 September 1868 in Chudenice in the Kingdom of Bohemia.\n- The Kingdom of Bohemia was a medieval and early modern monarchy in Central Europe.\n- The Kingdom of Bohemia was the predecessor of the modern Czech Republic.\n- Rusalka is an opera described as a lyric fairy tale by Antonín Dvořák.\n- Jaroslav Kvapil was a Czech poet, playwright, and librettist.\n- Jaroslav Kvapil died on 10 January 1950 in Prague.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
